{
 "carried": [
  {
   "chars": 1092,
   "heading": "3. The booster mesh",
   "sha256": "1fec595f47a9992e24fc671e92b15e447d4de51639aa4e7bd5f943d738c557f6",
   "text": "## 3. The booster mesh\n\n`RBatmobileBooster` (size 2400, super `RVehicleWeapon`) declares **only** `bBoosting`@2396, `bWarming`@2396. It is a weapon-shaped gadget with no mesh member; the mesh is on the archetype.\n\n| what | value | label |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Actor.Tag` | \"RBatmobileBooster\" | decoded |\n| `RInventoryGadget.Mesh` | `Batmobile_Booster.GadgetMesh` | decoded |\n| attach point (JC3 side) | socket `Afterburner` on bone `JetSMove` at ['-0.010', '0.538', '3.393'] (role afterburner) and `Afterburner_Front` on `Batmobile_Chassis_Mesh` at ['-0.000', '0.690', '-2.930'] | decoded (SOCKETS_JC3.md) |\n| what carries it in the build | the `Afterburner` socket's bone `JetSMove` is a **chassis** bone, not a part, and the socket's `part_hint` is `jet` - i.e. the game expects a jet *part* under that bone | decoded |\n| what is missing | a part in the donor chassis named/behaving as a jet, and the gadget mesh object itself (`Weapons.Batmobile_Booster.GadgetMesh`); the boost *force* is live (`arcade.nitro_boost` on the donor) but nothing is drawn | decoded (absence) / derived (the gap) |"
  },
  {
   "chars": 3024,
   "heading": "4. The JC3 house for tracker + missile + mesh",
   "sha256": "65493b6725e18931c31ddc011de70debf8f6ce607b0841e1d48cb74d125f1127",
   "text": "## 4. The JC3 house for tracker + missile + mesh\n\n### 4.1 What JC3 has, decoded\n\n| JC3 asset | value | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| weapon-owned force pulses | 25 pulses are owned by a `CMissileWeaponBase` and 29 by a `CBulletWeaponBase`, each using **that weapon's own** blast tune | FORCEPULSE.md §4.2 |\n| the EMP pulse | `EMP` -> `truck_emp.ftune`: PlayerDamage 100 / 25 m, held at full radius (`*PercentageMax` 1, `*Min` 1) vs a plain car blast 500 / 5 m | EMP.md §2 |\n| `CEMPWeapon` | `w702_emp` (handheld) and `w503_turret_emp` (turret) exist; **0** of the fleet's 88 vehicle weapon components is one | EMP.md §6 |\n| a target tag / allegiance switch | `allegian` appears in **0** of 295 entity dumps; `hack` in only 2 files (a SAM turret context-act animation) | HACKABLES.md §1 |\n| the HUD lock marker | `POI_TYPE_LOCK_ON_TARGET` = 21, rotating reticle 1.5 s/turn, plus `MCI_missile_locked` flashing 0.5 s - one type, one icon, no creation call in the movie | JC3_HUD_WEAPONS.md §5 |\n\n### 4.2 The routes, each with its label and its 5-minute experiment\n\n| # | route | what the files already give | label | next 5-minute experiment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 | missile weapon that owns the EMP pulse | a `CMissileWeaponBase` pulse is a decoded, shipped pattern (25 instances); put `truck_emp.ftune` on the Batmobile's missile component's pulse | decoded (pattern + tune) / derived (the pairing) | clone w618, point its `id:B5AE7986`-owned pulse at a copy of `truck_emp.ftune`, fire at an APC: is the victim visibly disabled? One file edit, one shot |\n| R2 | `CEMPWeapon` in a driver slot | class exists (`w702`/`w503`), 0 vehicle users; its tune has **no** EMP field, so the class alone decides | decoded (absence) / UNKNOWN (engine acceptance) | bind `w503_turret_emp` to one free driver slot on a copy entity and fire at a car; if the engine accepts, the disable comes free |\n| R3 | track-then-fire, i.e. the tag system | **no tag member exists** in JC3; the nearest decoded instruments are the AutoAim envelope (sticky aim, no lock time/range) and the HUD POI lock reticle | decoded (absence) / UNKNOWN (engine POI source) | fire `w609` at a car and watch whether `POI_TYPE_LOCK_ON_TARGET` ever appears without script: if the engine paints it from AutoAim, the *marker* half of the tracker is free |\n| R4 | the use-item graph (burst path, T-WP5b route c) | `entry.use_item` -> `S_STUNT_USE_ITEM_VEHICLE`, prompt `ui_activate_emp`; no pointer from trigger to pulse | decoded objects / UNKNOWN link | graft the graph + pulse onto a test car, press use-item: does the prompt appear and the pulse fire? |\n| R5 | draw the booster mesh | `Afterburner` socket on bone `JetSMove`, role afterburner; the boost itself is live | decoded (socket) / derived (route) | attach a placeholder mesh to a part parented to `JetSMove` and check the socket tracks the chassis in a replay, no game change needed |\n\nNothing here is a speculative implementation: each row names the object to copy and the one\nobservation that would settle it."
  },
  {
   "chars": 1740,
   "heading": "6. COMPROMISES (unapproved - the operator approves through Claude)",
   "sha256": "a72bbd03398a188873fbfa1c0e8a97eb0a5d3c51845da4a7c45185e9a3072484",
   "text": "## 6. COMPROMISES (unapproved - the operator approves through Claude)\n\n### C1 - the tag half of the tracker\n**What:** ship the tracker missile and the HUD lock marker, but not a tag that gates the missile.\n**Why:** JC3 has no tag/allegiance member on any vehicle (HACKABLES: `allegian` 0/295), so the\nlock would have to be a script-side convention.\n**Accuracy lost:** BmAK's core loop - mark once, then the EMP missile follows *that* car - becomes\n\"aim again for every shot\"; a tagged car cannot be remembered, and the untag failure prompt has\nno state to fire from.\n**RECOMMENDED COMPROMISE:** R1 + R3 marker only. It keeps the missile, the blast and the HUD\nreticle; it drops the memory of the tag.\n\n### C2 - the disable\n**What:** ship the Immobilizer as a missile whose impact pulse is `truck_emp.ftune` (100 dmg / 25 m).\n**Why:** the disable itself has no decoded member on either side; the pulse is the only EMP object\nthe fleet actually carries.\n**Accuracy lost:** if the pulse does not disable, the missile is a weak blast - the gadget's whole\npoint (T-WP4's original block).\n**RECOMMENDED COMPROMISE:** R1 first (one file edit), and only fall back to C2's plain blast if the\n5-minute shot shows no disable.\n\n### C3 - the booster mesh\n**What:** keep the donor's nitro force and add a jet part at the `Afterburner` socket without the\nBmAK gadget mesh.\n**Why:** the mesh object lives in BmAK's weapon packages and the donor chassis has no jet part.\n**Accuracy lost:** the flame/booster silhouette is a JC3 part, not BmAK's, so the rear of the car\nwill not match frame-for-frame.\n**RECOMMENDED COMPROMISE:** R5 placeholder now, T-12's part pass later - the socket is decoded,\nso the geometry can be swapped without moving anything else."
  },
  {
   "chars": 1136,
   "heading": "7. Reopened closures",
   "sha256": "e631f4de69fd826e36045b8fe85f1cea5f564d4b2d697dea5b8a7582c3f3149b",
   "text": "## 7. Reopened closures\n\n| row | old disposition | what this note changes | new status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-WP4 | blocked (\"the disable half cannot be built\") | the disable is not a member on **either** side, but a weapon-owned pulse is a shipped JC3 pattern (25 instances) and `CEMPWeapon` exists with 0 vehicle users: two live routes, one 5-minute shot each | **reopened** (routes R1/R2), disable still UNKNOWN |\n| T-WP5 | blocked (\"nothing fires it\") | unchanged by this note; T-WP5b already lists five routes and its own experiments | still open, owned by T-WP5b |\n| T-WP8 (sonar) | out (named omission) | untouched here - priority 5 in the operator's order | out, unchanged |\n| T-WP9 | out (\"no tracker class\") | the *class* absence is real, but the tracker is a launcher + a homing projectile + a tag field, and the launcher half has a JC3 carrier (w618 clone, R1); the tag half is what is missing (R3) | **reopened** as `partial`: carrier yes, gate no |\n| T-MD2 | blocked | same evidence as T-WP4: the launcher is mountable in both modes (`BattleModeFireButtonPressed`); the disable is the only gap | **reopened** with T-WP4 |"
  },
  {
   "chars": 356,
   "heading": "8. Checks",
   "sha256": "7251279dbdb98f4ca8354f7e16a67b03932a6b09d6b8090dc936c1938808ba5b",
   "text": "## 8. Checks\n\n`python Tools/scripts/t_wp4c.py --write` writes this file and the JSON; `--check` re-derives both\nand compares byte for byte; `--tamper-test` mutates (1) a field offset in the EMP class header,\n(2) a `LockOnTime` value in a runtime sample and (3) this file's own text, and asserts each is\nnoticed. Sources are listed at the top of the script."
  }
 ],
